2026-04-27 11:48:27,111 - __main__ - INFO - Retrieved process_rule for ID J09D: ('J09D', '1. Make a copy of decision_table with TOURS starting with J09D named J09D_temp\n2. Update the table with an additional empty column ENTSCHEIDUNG\n3. Apply the following rules to the joined table:\n   1. Count the number of EQUNR for every HAUS and set ENTSCHEIDUNG to "KSA" if there are less than 3 EQUNR. ELSE set ENTSCHEIDUNG to "EVU"\n   2. Set all houses with HOUSE_NUM1 of 0 to "EVU"\n   3. Set all houses with HOUSE_NUM1 500 - 599 to "EVU"\n   4. Set all houses with HOUSE_NUM1 900 - 999 to "EVU"\n   5. Set all houses with address area Wiblingwerde or Breckerfeld to "EVU"\n4. Join this table with the EABLG table using INSTALLATION\n5. Join this table with the NET_MASTER table and the SALES_MASTER table using EQUNR\n6. Compare sales data and net data for these IDs:\n   - If sales data is there, take sales data and empty net data\n   - Otherwise stay with net data and empty sales data\n7. Set ENTSCHEIDUNG to "MANDATORY_READING" for every EQUNR in EABL where both conditions are met:\n   - ISTABLART_TXT = "Maschinelle Schätzung - SAP" and the record was created in 2024\n   - ISTABLART_TXT = "Maschinelle Schätzung - SAP" and the record was created in 2023\n8. Export all MANDATORY_READING entries from the final table as CSV file named J09D_MANDATORY_READING including the columns: `Meter Reading (MR) Doc. No.`, `HAUS`, `ANLAGE`, `ME_MA_ID`, `EQUNR`, `HOUSE_NUM1`, `ENTSCHEIDUNG`, `TITLE`, `FORENAME`, `SURNAME`, `STREET`, `STREETNO`, `POST_CODE1`, `CITY1`, `CITY2`, `EMAIL`\n9. Send them to the internal team at mandatory.reading@provider.com\n10. Export the final data except MANDATORY_READING entries as CSV file named J09D including the columns: `Meter Reading (MR) Doc. No.`, `HAUS`, `ANLAGE`, `ME_MA_ID`, `EQUNR`, `HOUSE_NUM1`, `ENTSCHEIDUNG`, `TITLE`, `FORENAME`, `SURNAME`, `STREET`, `STREETNO`, `POST_CODE1`, `CITY1`, `CITY2`, `EMAIL`\n11. Send them to the EVU team at meter.readings@evu.com\n12. Delete the temporary table after exporting the data.')
