2026-04-27 13:10:12,960 - __main__ - INFO - Retrieved process_rule for ID J09D: ('J09D', '1. Copy the decision table into table `J09D_temp` for all records where the tour starts with `J09D`.\n\n2. Add column `ENTSCHEIDUNG` to `J09D_temp`.\n\n3. Classify the meter reading type in `ENTSCHEIDUNG` using these rules:\n   - If a `HAUS` has fewer than 3 `EQUNR`, set `ENTSCHEIDUNG = "KSA"`.\n   - Else set `ENTSCHEIDUNG = "EVU"`.\n   - Additionally, set all houses with `HOUSE_NUM1 = 0` to `ENTSCHEIDUNG = "EVU"`.\n\n4. JOIN `J09D_temp` with the `EABLG` table using `INSTALLATION`.\n\n5. JOIN the result with `SALES_MASTER` and `NET_MASTER` using `EQUNR`.\n\n6. Compare customer data from `SALES_MASTER` and `NET_MASTER`.\n\n7. If sales customer data is not empty:\n   1. Use the customer entries from the sales customer data table.\n   Else:\n   1. Use the customer entries from the net customer data table.\n\n8. Export the final table as CSV file named `J09D`.\n   Use exactly these column names in the export:\n   `Meter Reading (MR) Doc. No.`, `HAUS`, `ANLAGE`, `ME_MA_ID`, `EQUNR`, `HOUSE_NUM1`, `ENTSCHEIDUNG`, `TITLE`, `FORENAME`, `SURNAME`, `STREET`, `STREETNO`, `POST_CODE1`, `CITY1`, `CITY2`, `EMAIL`.\n\n9. Send an email to `meter.readings@evu.com` with the exported CSV file attached.\n   Use file path: `<path_to_exported_csv_file>`.\n\n10. Delete the temporary table.\n\n11. End the process.')
