2026-04-27 13:54:17,728 - __main__ - INFO - Retrieved process_rule for ID J09C: ('J09C', '1. Copy the decision table into table `J09C_temp` for all tours that start with `J09C`.\n\n2. Add column `ENTSCHEIDUNG` to table `J09C_temp`.\n\n3. Classify the meter reading type in `ENTSCHEIDUNG` using these rules:\n   - If a `HAUS` has less than 3 `EQUNR`, set `ENTSCHEIDUNG` to `KSA`; else set it to `EVU`.\n   - Set `ENTSCHEIDUNG` to `EVU` for all houses with `HOUSE_NUM1 = 0`.\n   - Set `ENTSCHEIDUNG` to `EVU` for all houses with `HOUSE_NUM1` from `500` to `599`.\n   - Set `ENTSCHEIDUNG` to `EVU` for all houses with `HOUSE_NUM1` from `900` to `999`.\n   - Set `ENTSCHEIDUNG` to `EVU` for all houses in address area `Wiblingwerde` or `Breckerfeld`.\n\n4. Join the current table with `EABLG` using `INSTALLATION`.\n\n5. Join the current table with `SALES_MASTER` and `NET_MASTER` using `EQUNR`.\n\n6. Compare customer data from `SALES_MASTER` and `NET_MASTER`.\n\n7. If sales customer data is not empty:\n   1. Use the customer entries from the sales customer data table.\n   Else:\n   1. Use the customer entries from the net customer data table.\n\n8. Export the final table as CSV file named `J09C`.\n   Use exactly these column names in the export:\n   - `Meter Reading (MR) Doc. No.`\n   - `HAUS`\n   - `ANLAGE`\n   - `ME_MA_ID`\n   - `EQUNR`\n   - `HOUSE_NUM1`\n   - `ENTSCHEIDUNG`\n   - `TITLE`\n   - `FORENAME`\n   - `SURNAME`\n   - `STREET`\n   - `STREETNO`\n   - `POST_CODE1`\n   - `CITY1`\n   - `CITY2`\n   - `EMAIL`\n\n9. Send an email with the CSV file to EVU.\n   - Email address: `meter.readings@evu.com`\n   - `file_path: <path_to_exported_csv_file>`\n\n10. Delete the temporary table.')
